# Single worker process, 8 threads: a free workaround for the rate
# limiter's per-worker counters (see RATE_LIMIT_STORAGE_URI in app.py) —
# gunicorn threads share one process's memory, so memory:// storage is
# actually correct again with --workers 1, at the cost of losing
# multi-core parallelism for CPU-bound plan computation. Once a real
# shared store (Redis) is provisioned, set RATE_LIMIT_STORAGE_URI/
# REDIS_URL and raise --workers back up — the limiter code already
# supports that without further changes.
web: gunicorn --workers 1 --threads 8 --timeout 60 --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT app:app
